# The single source of truth for the two-grain boundary.
# Companion plan: external-research/20260808-045124_two-grains-template-breach-and-code-distillation-plan.md
# Root-nesting plan:  external-research/20260808-183336_the-compact-root-nesting-for-a-public-seed.md
#
# Every tracked root path carries exactly one verdict:
#   template — copied verbatim into the public seed (grain-os/grain)
#   scrub    — copied only after the name->role / Acme-voice transform (.claude/rules/acme-employee-voice.md)
#   personal — never copied; lives only in the private field
#
# FAIL-SAFE: when a path's contents are uncertain, it is personal (withhold).
# A privacy boundary built additively cannot leak what it never received.
#
# A `scrub` directory may still hold individual `personal` files that the
# projection must exclude by sub-path; those are named in the sub-exclude
# section at the foot. The projection tool (proposed tools/sow.rish) reads
# this file and its witness proves: no personal path, no real key, no real
# name ever appears in the projected seed.

# ---- dotfiles and root config ----
template  .brix                          # root Brix descriptor
template  .cursorignore                  # editor ignore posture
template  .gitattributes                 # attribute rules
template  .gitignore                     # allowlist posture — exactly what a template wants
template  .gitmodules                    # gratitude/ and vendor/ submodule pins only
template  .vscode                        # editor settings, no personal data
template  template-manifest.bron         # this file — the boundary's own definition (withheld anyway: lists keys_xykj61_* names)
scrub     .claude                        # rules name the maintainer as decision authority (session-logs, collaboration, riyo)
scrub     .cursor                        # Cursor twins of the same rules

# ---- root files ----
scrub     README.md                      # names the living identity in its foot
scrub     MAP.md                          # identity line + Keaton by name
scrub     SOURCE.md                       # onboarding guide; names the maintainer
scrub     CLAUDE.md                       # project instructions; heavy identity + voice
scrub     CONTRIBUTING.md                 # may name; commit-shape guidance
scrub     ORGANIZING.md                   # names the keeper throughout
scrub     bibliography.md                 # source gathering; scrub any naming
scrub     llms.txt                        # model-facing map; scrub identity
scrub     LICENSE-APACHE                  # copyright holder is a real name
scrub     LICENSE-MIT                     # copyright holder is a real name
scrub     LICENSE-CC-BY                   # copyright holder is a real name
template  GLOW_HOST.template.bron          # the withheld-fill-in template itself
template  GLOW_PROFILE.template.bron       # the withheld-fill-in template itself
template  PUBKEYS.template.md              # the withheld-fill-in template itself
personal  PUBKEYS.md                       # real SSH + OpenPGP fingerprints
personal  SAFE.md                          # custody by real name
personal  STEWARDS.md                      # steward mapping by real name
personal  keys_menlo_xykj61_landscape.png  # real identity key card
personal  keys_menlo_xykj61_portrait.png   # real identity key card
personal  keys_xykj61_contact_email.svg    # real contact card
personal  keys_xykj61_openpgp.svg          # real key card
personal  keys_xykj61_ssh_github.svg       # real key card

# ---- language and system code (the template's heart) ----
template  amphora                         # module
template  aurora                          # boot
template  brushstroke                     # drawing
template  caravan                         # supervision
template  cellar                          # module
template  comlink                         # device wire
template  glow                            # the Glow language implementation (nock nests here per the compact-root plan)
template  granary                         # module
template  dimeroll                      # module
template  lantern                         # inference lantern
template  lattice                         # module
template  mand                            # authority
template  mandate                         # vector store (turbopuffer) — clean code, no name; fake example vectors
template  mandi                           # module
template  mantra                          # versions
template  mycelium                        # module
template  ember                           # module
template  pond                            # enclosure
template  rishi                           # the shell language
template  rye                             # the systems language
template  scribble                        # module
template  scribe                          # the Kyri reader — clean code, no name
template  src                             # Glow userland (five rooms)
template  tally                           # bounded allocation
template  tools                           # witnesses and gates; gitignored secrets never enter; scrub any name on touch

# ---- code modules that name the maintainer in comments (scrub the name, ship the code) ----
scrub     kumara                          # identity module — tilak comments name the maintainer
scrub     settlement                      # settlement ledger — a comment names the maintainer

# ---- disciplines and design corpus (scrub: technical, yet name-bearing) ----
scrub     context                         # disciplines + specs + identity (RIYO/QUIN) — scrub identity, keep law
scrub     active-designing                # design corpus names the maintainer as decision authority
scrub     active-reviving                 # revival corpus, same
scrub     expanded-prompts                # cold records (past); name-heavy like expanding-prompts; batons sub-excluded personal
scrub     expanding-prompts               # runnable plans; name-heavy per the audit
scrub     waymarks                        # claim shelf; name-heavy per the audit
scrub     foundations                     # the why — doctrine ships (scrubbed); bio withheld file-granular (see sub-exclude)
scrub     linengrow                       # civic-app pattern (template) — yet holds venture specifics; see sub-exclude

# ---- teaching and study ----
template  docs                            # compressor pages; cite witnesses
template  docs-geode                      # teaching
template  edu                             # the learning floor
template  manual                          # the four teaching rooms
template  nixos-guide                     # host setup guide
scrub     external-research               # study of the world; name-bearing memos — scrub identity
template  gratitude                       # third-party, held whole and unmodified
template  vendor                          # third-party build source, unmodified

# ---- personal record (never copied) ----
personal  session-logs                    # years of reasoning traces that name the maintainer by design
personal  counsel                         # decision records — "on the maintainer's word"
personal  bron-resins                     # compressed personal reasoning trails
personal  work-in-progress                # the live operator cards of one maintainer
personal  press                           # personal announcements — name change, fund, ventures
personal  saga                            # season-close narratives, one steward's arc
personal  classical-vedic-astrology       # a personal-life study library, privacy-gated
personal  rye-learning-process            # a personal learning almanac
personal  keys                            # identity QR cards and key material

# ---- sub-exclude: paths withheld even though their verdict is scrub ----
# An entry is either a whole path or a single file inside a scrub directory.
# A file is withheld when it equals an entry or lives under one. This lets the
# foundations DOCTRINE ship (scrubbed) while the biography beside it stays home
# (Keaton's word 20260808 — share the doctrine, withhold only the bio).
# `context` is NOT here — its gitignored personal overrides (a real PUBKEYS.md,
# a filled GLOW_*.bron) are already untracked, so git ls-files never offers them.

# whole-path:
sub_exclude linengrow     # civic-app venture/treasury specifics tied to one person

# foundations biography (file-granular) — the doctrine beside these ships:
sub_exclude foundations/20260730-022147_keaton-livermore-resume-draft.md   # a resume
sub_exclude foundations/20260730-022147_personal-ontology.md               # personal ontology
sub_exclude foundations/20260730-022147_cover-letter-co-authored.md        # a cover letter
sub_exclude foundations/20260729-220100_the-names-we-did-not-use.md        # personal naming history

